<BaseLayout title="About" description="About APT Notes and its relationship to Hecavex."><article class="shell narrow prose"><p class="eyebrow">About the product</p><h1>APT Notes</h1><p class="lead">A structured knowledge base of threat actors and their operations.</p><p>APT Notes is a source-driven intelligence catalogue for searching, filtering and pivoting between threat actors, aliases, campaigns, malware, tools, targeting, techniques and attribution claims.</p><p>It is a separate product from <a href="https://hecavex.com/en/">Hecavex Research ↗</a>, which remains the publication for long-form investigations, analysis and commentary.</p><h2>What it is not</h2><p>APT Notes is not a live threat feed, detection service, SIEM, vulnerability scanner, authoritative attribution body or replacement for MITRE ATT&amp;CK.</p><h2>Editorial approach</h2><p>Source claims are separated from APT Notes assessments. Alias overlap is represented explicitly, uncertainty is retained, and corrections appear in the public change history.</p><p><a href="/about/methodology/">Read the complete methodology →</a></p></article></BaseLayout>
